# Karshak

Karshak is a full-stack farmer-to-consumer marketplace designed to connect
farmers directly with buyers and simplify the discovery, listing, and
purchase of agricultural products.

## Tech Stack

### Frontend
- React
- Vite
- JavaScript
- Axios

### Backend
- Node.js
- Express.js
- Prisma ORM
- PostgreSQL

## Repository Structure

```text
karshak/
├── client/     # React frontend
├── server/     # Express backend and database layer
└── README.md
```

## Core Features

- Farmer and buyer user flows
- Product listing and management
- Product categories and discovery
- Shopping and checkout flow
- Order management
- Authentication and authorization
- Image uploads
- PostgreSQL persistence using Prisma

## Architecture

The frontend communicates with the Express REST API, which handles
application logic and interacts with PostgreSQL through Prisma ORM.

```
React Client
     |
     | HTTP / REST
     v
Express API
     |
     v
Prisma ORM
     |
     v
PostgreSQL
```

## Project Status

Karshak was developed as an end-to-end full-stack marketplace project,
covering frontend development, backend APIs, database design, authentication,
deployment, and application workflows.